index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bf1a4aaa78c797c845c98fd669483a096f9da907
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/dev/backend/02-nvidia-executable.md
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+# NVIDIA executable and current-stream contract
+
+`NvidiaExecutable` is the process-owned runtime counterpart of immutable
+compiler `Artifact` data. It does not reuse TensorIR's `CudaTileRuntimeKernel`:
+that type owns unsynchronized mutable handles, has incomplete support/workspace
+checks, and cannot establish the PyPTO process/device/context lifetime law.
+
+The public type belongs to `pypto.runtime.nvidia`; CUDA types remain private.
+Construction takes one already validated `Artifact` and its `CompileRequest`,
+checks their byte-compile identity, and performs no CUDA call, file access,
+compilation, cache lookup, allocation or stream query. `KernelBuildSpec` is no
+longer needed after it has been transitively bound into the immutable Artifact.
+
+## Prewarm and loader compatibility
+
+`prewarm(active_cuda_runtime_api_version)` is the only load transaction. The
+runtime version is an explicit parent-provided observation—for example from the
+CUDA Runtime already loaded by PyTorch. The private Driver-only loader never
+loads a second `libcudart`.
+
+Prewarm is once-only and failure-latched. It:
+
+1. rejects a post-`fork` inherited object;
+2. lazily opens only the installed `libcuda.so.1` driver;
+3. verifies the minimum Driver and caller-supplied Runtime API versions;
+4. requires a non-null regular current context, rejects a current green
+   context, and records its stable context identity;
+5. verifies the current device ordinal, UUID, PCI identity, SM120 identity and
+   queryable resources against `CompileRequest.target_info`;
+6. loads the exact Cubin with context-bound `cuModule*` APIs and resolves only
+   `entry_function_name`;
+7. forces lazy function loading before capture;
+8. validates flattened parameter widths, binary target, block/shared-memory/
+   register/cluster limits and nonzero occupancy; and
+9. publishes `Ready` only after the complete transaction succeeds.
+
+Any partial module is rolled back on failure. The first bounded error is
+latched, no retry/fallback occurs, and all concurrent prewarm callers observe
+the same result. TensorIR, TileIR JIT, PTX, cuBLAS and framework fallback are
+not loader alternatives.
+
+Artifact v1 currently emits only static workspace size `0`, alignment `1`.
+Because it has no mapping from a workspace address to a kernel parameter, the
+loader rejects every nonzero workspace instead of allocating unused memory.
+
+## Prepared launch packet
+
+Argument validation and packing happen in `prepare_launch()` before graph
+capture. It returns a move-only `NvidiaLaunchPacket` owning stable, pre-sized
+eight-byte host slots, the parameter-pointer array and checked final grid.
+The packet itself is an execution lease and prevents unload.
+
+Tensor operands provide a non-null opaque device address plus complete shape
+and element-stride metadata. Static dimensions/strides must match exactly;
+dynamic values are packed according to the uniform/non-uniform Artifact ABI.
+Runtime grids use checked ceil division and multiplication. Scalar operands
+carry one through eight raw value bytes, copied into a zeroed slot.
+
+Artifact v1 does not encode tensor dtype, data-pointer alignment, address space
+or access mode. The executable can therefore validate pointer presence and
+shape/stride/parameter ABI only. Typed `pypto-kernels` and framework adapters
+must validate those missing properties before preparing a packet; this layer
+does not claim them.
+
+## Launch, graph lease and unload
+
+`launch(packet, raw_current_stream)` rejects the null, legacy-default and
+per-thread-default special stream handles. Every call revalidates creator
+process, current context identity/device and the stream's own context, then
+enqueues exactly once through `cuLaunchKernelEx`. The stream exists only as a
+stack-local argument and is never stored. CUDA green-context streams are
+rejected by v1.
+
+Launch success means only that enqueue was accepted. The executable creates no
+event, synchronization, allocation, retry or fallback. A packet must remain
+alive until its asynchronous work can no longer reference the module.
+
+`acquire_cuda_graph_lease()` is a move-only module lifetime lease. The graph
+owner retains it through instantiated-graph destruction; it stores no stream
+and does not itself prove CUDA Graph capture/replay correctness.
+
+Explicit `unload()` is terminal for that object and requires the bound current
+context plus zero active launches, packets and graph leases. Destruction never
+switches a framework context. If explicit cleanup was omitted and the bound
+context is unavailable, best-effort destruction leaks safely until context
+teardown instead of unloading in another context or a forked child.
+
+## Product boundary
+
+The implementation is a PyPTO-owned internal runtime object boundary embedded
+in the single `pypto_core` DSO. Backend-ON dynamically resolves the Driver;
+backend-OFF retains the CUDA-free public data/lifecycle surface and fails before
+driver loading. Neither product links `libcuda`, `libcudart`, TensorIR runtime,
+NVRTC or an external compute library.
+
+CPU fake-driver tests prove lifecycle, packing, arithmetic, failure and lease
+behavior separately from the required exclusive RTX 5090 non-default-stream
+smoke. They do not prove real Cubin loading, numerical correctness, CUDA Graph,
+framework integration, Qwen coverage or performance.
